{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790963495,"nonce":"NxJB+aLy2wncOAEzGmOnCRly7uc=","message":"Reproduced without xwindow: one primitive that throws a string through `hl_throw`. Both ~/.ash/bin/ash (Sep 28) and target/release/ash (Oct 2) print \"hlp_throw called without active trap; aborting\", then \"after the raise: not caught\".\n\nCargo.toml (cdylib, dependency hl_abi; on Apple link with `-Wl,-undefined,dynamic_lookup`), src/lib.rs:\n\n    use hl_abi::vdynamic;\n\n    unsafe extern \"C\" {\n        fn hl_alloc_strbytes(format: *const u16, ...) -\u003e *mut vdynamic;\n        fn hl_throw(value: *mut vdynamic) -\u003e !;\n    }\n\n    unsafe extern \"C\" fn raise() {\n        let message: Vec\u003cu16\u003e = \"raised by a native\".encode_utf16().chain([0]).collect();\n        unsafe { hl_throw(hl_alloc_strbytes(message.as_ptr())) }\n    }\n\n    hl_abi::define_prim!(hlp_raise, raise, \"P_v\");\n\nMain.hx, run with the library copied beside it as raise.hdll:\n\n    private extern class Native {\n        @:hlNative(\"raise\", \"raise\") public static function raise():Void;\n    }\n\n    class Main {\n        static function main() {\n            try {\n                Native.raise();\n                trace(\"after the raise: not caught\");\n            } catch (e:Dynamic) {\n                trace(\"caught: \" + e);\n            }\n        }\n    }","files":null}]}